+# TiKV-surfaced DST seed registry (the compounding loop)
+
+**Status: OPEN — no real-cluster discovery has been promoted yet.** This registry is
+the *target* for the compounding loop (proposal 0015 §"DST and tests"; architecture
+§13.1; the FoundationDB/TigerBeetle pattern), not a closed DoD bullet.
+
+## What the compounding loop requires (mandatory DoD, not optional)
+
+Every behaviour the **real** TiKV cluster surfaces under the M4.6 Tier-1/Jepsen/Tier-2
+runs (`cargo xtask meta-jepsen` / `meta-integration` / `meta-tier2`, `WYRD_TIER1=1`)
+that the redb fake did **not** model — a txn-conflict timing, a PD timestamp-oracle
+edge, a fault shape — is promoted back into DST as a **committed seeded regression**,
+wherever it manifests through the `MetadataStore` trait contract. DST keeps correctness
+authority; the real tiers never cede it.
+
+## Why this file is a registry and not an executable seed (the honest boundary)
+
+An executable DST regression is authored in the **slice-7 / #258** second-implementation
+contract harness (`crates/dst`), and it can only encode a *real* discovery once the
+privileged, off-Check Tier job has produced one. Within this slice's boundary:
+
+- Re-deriving exactly-one-winner over the redb/in-memory fake would **re-prove Tier-0's
+  own atomicity** — the invariant "a real environment is never used to test correctness
+  the simulation already covers" forbids it (and this was the iteration-1 defect).
+- A DST test built on a *copy* of the TiKV commit protocol passes vacuously (drives a
+  copy, not production) — explicitly forbidden.
+- A genuine seed requires editing the metadata backend (`crates/metadata-tikv/src`),
+  which is **outside this slice's surface**.
+
+So: **no executable seed is committed here, and this document does not by itself close
+the compounding-loop DoD bullet.** It is a NEEDS-HUMAN item (brief Known NEEDS-HUMAN #5)
+— the human either accepts the deferral to #258 *after* a real discovery is recorded
+below from a live run, or holds the bullet open. This is the iteration-3 direction:
+"deferring the executable DST regression to #258 is acceptable, but only once a
+real-cluster discovery exists to promote; a known-gap hypothesis doc alone does not
+close the mandatory DoD bullet."
+
+## Promotion protocol (how a live discovery becomes a seed)
+
+When a Tier job surfaces an unmodeled behaviour, record it here as `SURFACED-<n>` with:
+its provenance (the recorded fault schedule + history-check verdict), the trait-level
+observation, and the `#258` seed id + `MADSIM_TEST_SEED` once the executable regression
+lands. Until then this list is intentionally empty.
+
+| id | provenance (live run) | trait-level observation | #258 seed | status |
+|----|-----------------------|-------------------------|-----------|--------|
+| _(none yet)_ | — | — | — | awaiting a privileged Tier-job run |
